# HR-012: Remote Work Policy

**Document ID:** HR-012
**Title:** Remote Work Policy
**Version:** 1.0
**Effective Date:** January 1, 2025
**Owner:** HR & People Department (Rachel Williams, CHRO)

---

## 1. Policy Purpose and Scope

This policy establishes the guidelines and expectations for remote work arrangements at **MedSync Health**, a leading healthcare technology company founded in **January 2019**. As a Series D company preparing for an IPO, MedSync Health recognizes the value of flexibility in attracting and retaining top talent across our global footprint, which includes offices in **Boston, MA (HQ)**, **London, UK**, **Berlin, Germany**, and **Singapore**.

This policy applies to all **1,200** employees of MedSync Health, regardless of their location or employment status, and is subject to the general provisions outlined in **HR-001: General Employee Policies**.

## 2. Remote Work Models

MedSync Health primarily operates on a **Hybrid-First Model**, balancing the benefits of in-person collaboration with the flexibility of remote work.

| Model | Description | Required In-Office Presence |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Hybrid** | Employees work a portion of their time in a designated MedSync Health office and a portion remotely. | Minimum 2 days per week, or as determined by department leadership. |
| **Fully Remote** | Employees work exclusively from a location outside a MedSync Health office. | Requires specific approval and is limited to roles where physical presence is not essential. |
| **Occasional** | Ad-hoc remote work for specific, short-term needs (e.g., appointments, home repairs). | Requires manager approval on a case-by-case basis. |

## 3. Eligibility and Approval Criteria

Eligibility for remote work is determined by the nature of the role, the employee's performance, and their organizational level, reflecting the varying leadership and mentorship responsibilities across the company.

### 3.1. Eligibility by Employee Level

| Employee Level | Remote Work Eligibility | In-Office Expectation | Average Compensation (AED) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Individual Contributor (IC)** | Eligible for Hybrid or Fully Remote (role-dependent). | Flexible, minimum 2 days/week for Hybrid roles. | **294,000** |
| **Manager** | Eligible for Hybrid. Fully Remote requires VP approval. | Minimum 3 days/week to ensure team cohesion and mentorship. | **441,000** |
| **Director** | Eligible for Hybrid. Fully Remote is rare and requires CHRO approval. | Minimum 4 days/week to maintain strong cross-departmental leadership. | **661,500** |
| **VP and C-Level** | Primarily In-Office/HQ-Based. Occasional remote work only. | Required to be based near the **Boston, MA (HQ)** or a major regional office to ensure strategic alignment. | **1,102,500** (VP Avg.) |

### 3.2. Approval Process

1.  The employee submits a Remote Work Request Form to their direct Manager.
2.  The Manager reviews the request, considering team needs and performance.
3.  For Fully Remote requests, the request is escalated to the Department Head (VP) for final review.
4.  All Fully Remote arrangements must be formally approved by the CHRO, Rachel Williams.

## 4. Remote Work Environment and Equipment

MedSync Health is committed to ensuring a productive and secure remote work environment.

### 4.1. Equipment Stipend

To support the establishment of a suitable home office, eligible employees will receive a one-time remote work stipend. This stipend is set at **AED 7,350** (a number symbolically linked to our initial Seed funding round in January 2019, which was AED 7,350,000).

### 4.2. Security and Compliance

All remote work must adhere to MedSync Health's security protocols. Employees must ensure their remote workspace is secure and compliant with all relevant regulations, including **HIPAA Compliance** (certified March 2020), **SOC 2 Type II** (renewed August 2024), and **GDPR Compliance** (implemented May 2020).

